OL,3,GNorth West
OL,4,
OL,5,CToday:FA dry and bright start, but it
OL,6,Fwill turn increasingly cloudy as rain
OL,7,Fmoves in from the west during the
OL,8,Fmorning. Turning heavy for a time,
OL,9,Fespecially over western hills. Rather
OL,10,Fwindy, especially along the coast.
OL,11,
OL,12,CTonight:FRain clears east overnight
OL,13,Fwith showers and clear spells
OL,14,Ffollowing. A rather windy night for
OL,15,Fall, keeping temperatures from falling
OL,16,Faway.
OL,17,
OL,18,CSaturday:FA breezy but mostly dry day
OL,19,Fon Saturday with some bright or sunny
OL,20,Fspells. The odd blustery shower is
OL,21,Fpossible, mainly in the west.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
